# How to cite Zhen. GitHub reads this file and offers it as "Cite this repository".
#
# No `version` or `date-released`, on purpose: ZhenVersion.swift is the only declaration of
# the version, and a second copy here would go stale at the first release that forgot it.
# Someone citing a particular release names it from the tag.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Zhen in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Zhen: a fast, native network scanner for macOS"
abstract: >-
  A network scanner written entirely in Swift 6: the engine, the zhen command line, and
  the privileged helper, as one Swift package. It sweeps a /24 in about three seconds by
  retransmitting early and declaring late, names devices through Bonjour, NetBIOS and
  UPnP, and states plainly what it could not work out and why.
authors:
  - name: "zhen-swift"
    website: "https://github.com/zhen-swift"
# Who started it, kept out of the citation itself: tools format `authors` only.
contact:
  - given-names: "Juan Carlos"
    family-names: "Estévez Rodríguez"
repository-code: "https://github.com/zhen-swift/zhen-core"
url: "https://github.com/zhen-swift/zhen-core"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - network scanner
  - host discovery
  - port scanning
  - macOS
  - Swift
